{"records":[{"id":"vhzzzc6m36","title":"Diagnostic Discrimination of Zika and Dengue-2 Infection by High-Throughput TCR Sequencing","description":"The Zika virus has been listed as a global health threat by the World Health Organization due to its association with congenital birth defects. Current FDA-approved diagnostics are unable to distinguish between infection with Zika and other flaviviruses. Here, we report on the computational identification of virus-associated TCRβ-sequencing using high-throughput sequencing prior to and after infection with Zika or Dengue-2 viruses.  Computationally identified T cell receptor sequences were shown to be virus-specific and used to develop a diagnostic assay that correctly diagnoses Zika and Dengue-2 infected in mice with 97% accuracy. These results identify populations of TCR sequences specific for Zika and Dengue infection that can be used for diagnostic purposes, and serve as an important proof-of-principle, providing a novel platform for accurately diagnosing Zika virus infection. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2019-09-25T17:03:23.996Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/vhzzzc6m36","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/vhzzzc6m36"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kyle","last_name":"Wolf","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["DNA Sequencing"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"d7kjy4vmm6","title":"Towards an improved platform for dengue and Zika virus virus-like particle production ","description":"FAME analysis Using GC-QTOF with HP-88 (100m) column for the manuscript entitled Towards an improved platform for dengue and Zika virus virus-like particle production ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-06-10T16:20:53.712Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/d7kjy4vmm6","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/d7kjy4vmm6"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Atikorn","last_name":"Panya","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Duncan","last_name":"Smith","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Suwipa","last_name":"Ramphan","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Nathamon","last_name":"Yimpring","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Chontida","last_name":"Tangsongcharoen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Suthatta","last_name":"Sornprasert","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Sittiruk","last_name":"Roytrakul","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Zika Virus","Dengue Virus","Fatty Acid Methyl Ester"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"6yvtysrwfv","title":"Freppel_2024_metabolomics","description":"Raw data of the GC/MS acquisition for the metabolites shown in Fig 4G of Freppel et al manuscript entitled: \"Dengue virus and Zika virus alter endoplasmic reticulum-mitochondria contact sites to\nregulate respiration and apoptosis\", published in iScience. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-11-18T11:21:29.217Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/6yvtysrwfv","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/6yvtysrwfv"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Laura","last_name":"Hulea","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01gavpb45","name":"Canadian Institutes of Health Research","grant_id":"PJT153020"}],"categories":["Metabolomics"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"y6xjbjcgz8","title":"Docking of Dengue virus type 1 or West Nile Virus surface antigen with SARS-CoV-2 Spike antibody","description":"Docking of SARS-CoV-2 Spike antibody with surface antigen of Dengue virus type 1 or West Nile Virus using ClusPro and ZDOCK","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-11-09T09:56:09.616Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/y6xjbjcgz8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/y6xjbjcgz8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Subhajit","last_name":"Biswas","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Virology","West Nile Virus","Dengue Virus","COVID-19"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ks44dmkgnj","title":"Influence of previous Zika virus infection on acute dengue episode","description":"It is a dataset related to 2019 dengue outbreak.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-01-28T15:38:58.639Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ks44dmkgnj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ks44dmkgnj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Cassia","last_name":"Estofolete","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":null,"name":"INCT Viral Genomic Surveillance and One Health","grant_id":"405786/2022-0"},{"id":null,"name":"INCT dengue program","grant_id":"465425/2014-3"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"U01AI151807"},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","grant_id":"2018/17647-0"},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","grant_id":"2022/03645-1"},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","grant_id":"2022/09229-0"}],"categories":["Infectious Disease","Clinical Virology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"cv9c4gzdy9","title":"S5. Transmission potenital (Index P) data","description":"Transmission potential (index P)  quantifies the risk of dengue virus transmission in a specific region, taking into account climate-based factors such as temperature and humidity, which directly influence the breeding, survival, and biting behaviour of the mosquito vectors responsible for spreading the virus. This index provides insight into how favourable environmental conditions are for dengue circulation in a given area.  The spatio-temporal estimates of transmission potential for African countries and territories used in this review were developed by Nakase et. al (2023) .","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-10-17T09:43:47.366Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/cv9c4gzdy9","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/cv9c4gzdy9"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Gaspary","last_name":"Mwanyika","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/05bk57929","name":"Stellenbosch University","grant_id":null}],"categories":["Systematic Review"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"wndgmzfbgc","title":"Biblio-HUB: a reproducible bibliometric workflow for aligning arbovirus research output with disease burden","description":"Source numerical data underlying the main figures and robustness analyses: a cross-viral summary of surveillance scope, Spearman correlations, OLS R2 and standardized coefficients; country-level cumulative cases, publications, residuals and gap flags for chikungunya, Zika, dengue and West Nile virus; per-capita rates; World Bank population and GDP per capita; and annual global publication counts. Web of Science records are not included because they are proprietary to Clarivate.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-11-01T16:42:45.058Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/wndgmzfbgc","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/wndgmzfbgc"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jing","last_name":"Li","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Information System","Virology","Epidemiologist"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"y2x7c6x76n","title":"Emerging therapy for dengue","description":"Dengue fever is acute febrile diseases, it’s caused by one of four closely related virus serotypes of the genusare Flavi virus, family Flaviviridae. Each serotype is sufficiently different that there is no cross-protection and epidemics caused by multiple serotypes can occurs. It’s transmitted to humans by the mosquito.\nThe incidence of dengue has grown around the world in recent a period of ten years. However, several classes of agents are in under investigation as potential anti-dengue drugs, including direct host modulators, antivirals, and RNAi therapeutics. These anti-dengue drugs in development will be reviewed here.\nKeywords: Dengue viruses, Aedes mosquito, Treatment\n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-05-31T06:11:11.028Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/y2x7c6x76n","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/y2x7c6x76n"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jitesh N patil","last_name":"Narendra patil","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Dengue Virus"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"x4msbrdgth","title":"Sex-specific effect of antenatal Zika virus infection on murine fetal growth, placental nutrient transporters, and nutrient sensor signaling pathways 2","description":"The present data supports the findings of the study titled ´Sex-specific effect of antenatal Zika virus infection on murine fetal growth, placental nutrient transporters, and nutrient sensor signaling pathways´.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-05-31T08:16:18.806Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/x4msbrdgth","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/x4msbrdgth"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Daniela","last_name":"Pereira-Carvalho","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Placenta","Zika Virus"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"s3xw35xczs","title":"Disrupting the HDAC6-ubiquitin interaction impairs infection by influenza and Zika virus and cellular stress pathways","description":"The original data for manuscript: \"Disrupting the HDAC6-ubiquitin interaction impairs infection by influenza and Zika virus and cellular stress pathways\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-08-18T12:11: